{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 120,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you watch MinutePhysics, chances are you\nlike science, or you like the internet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4660,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here's a list of some of the most consistently\nawesome and creative science storytellers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8440,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explainers and teachers that I've encountered\nonline - it's by no means exhaustive and there's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12420,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot more great science content out there,\nbut this is what consistently catches my attention!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16400,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "xkcd and the spinoff blog, \"xkcd what if?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20420,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "set a gold standard to which I continually\naspire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23270,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The comic Saturday Morning Breakfast Cereal\ntears science down in a sometimes-innapropriate-for-children"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27950,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but always hilariously nerdy way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30130,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Empirical Zeal is an eminently understandable\nblog about physics - Which Sean Carroll also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "writes about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35920,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He's sometimes technical, but also deep and\ninsightful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38980,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Terry Tao has a seriously technical - and\nI mean seriously - but also fascinating blog"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43800,
    "dDurationMs": 1449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about pure mathematics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45249,
    "dDurationMs": 4501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tumblr and facebook have their places, too,\nwith It's Ok To Be Smart and I pilcrow hash"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49750,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at asterisk-ing love science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51910,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since long before tumblr, The NASA Astronomy\npicture of the day has been a consistently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56070,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "awe-inspiring window onto the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58690,
    "dDurationMs": 2349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Radiolab is science radio at its best."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61039,
    "dDurationMs": 4001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might even go so far as to say it's radio\nat its best that just happens to be about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65040,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66040,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to get your hands dirty, Hyper\nPhysics is basically a condensed encyclopedia"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69540,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of high school or early college-level physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72260,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Scale of Universe is a modern-day interactive\nversion of the classic \"powers of ten\" film"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76320,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it shows you just how big and how small\nthings in the universe really are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80500,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, Microsoft has finally gotten itself\na point in my book for digitally hosting \"The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84600,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Character of Physical Law\", a wonderful series\nof lectures given by Richard Feynman in 1964."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88670,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, what about youtube?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90510,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, for physics there's Veritasium and Sixty\nSymbols; for chemistry check out Periodic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94920,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Videos or Crash Course; for zoology and the\nlives of dead animals there's The Brain Scoop;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99610,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for real and hands on science visit Smarter\nEvery Day; Vi Hart will wow you with beautiful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104430,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematics and George Hart will build beautiful\nmathematics and Numberphile will remind you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108540,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there are numbers in math, too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110490,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For generally random cool facts try Vsauce\nor TED Ed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114000,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in case you need a breather from it all,\nFake Science is a good reminder that sometimes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117710,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science is a bit too important to be taken\nseriously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120720,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've included links to all these great creators\nin the video description, but beware - they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124710,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bring procrastination!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
